{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Mamzer.</b> The Sages said: one born of forbidden sexual relations. The second [view adds] extra mems like ממין; some say ממזר from מגורות. Others said it is the name of a nation, as in וישב ממזר באשדוד, for it is far-fetched that an Israelite would be called by a derogatory name, even in the time of salvation. And the translator [Targum] took a shortcut and interpreted it:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כי רחוק הוא שיקרא שם ישראל' likely refers to the difficulty in identifying the Israelite context of the word; 'השני' may refer to a second view among the Sages or to a second element of etymological analysis."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:28.472003479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}